            <ArticleTitle>The Evolution of Pediatric Disease-A Moving Target in Public Health.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">E18</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3390/diseases5030018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is a growing threat in the re-emergence of diseases that impact pediatric demographics. While major strides have been made in the field of childhood cancers, there are still more questions than answers. In addition, public resistance to recommended practices related to childhood vaccinations fueled by misinformation has allowed infectious diseases to resurface in developed nations. Meanwhile, climate change and other destabilizing factors are shifting vector populations and driving the emergence of new diseases. Herein we call upon the community of human health researchers to confront the evolving specter of pediatric disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
